      "author": "itvision",
      "published": "2026-08-06T20:23:11Z",
      "bullets": [
        "AMD acquired Taalas to build hardwired AI ASICs, directly etching neural network model architectures and weights into custom silicon.",
        "Etching weights eliminates DRAM memory bandwidth bottlenecks, dramatically improving AI inference speed, latency, and power efficiency compared to GPUs.",
        "This fixed-function approach trades model mutability for extreme compute density, targeting high-volume, standardized foundation model deployments."
